{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Misim</b> [is] plural, and the singular is mas, like <i>fattim</i> (Leviticus 2:6) [and] <i>fat</i> (Genesis 18:5), and they are of the reduplication patterns." "And the meaning of <i>'anoto</i> [is] to dry up the seed of the males." "<b>Miskenot.</b> Storehouses, and like it <i>el ha-soken</i> (Isaiah 22:15) and <i>vat’hi la-melekh sokenet</i> (I Kings 1:4), the keeper of the storehouse, 'and she did not know anything and lay in your bosom.'" "<b>Ra'mses.</b> With a pataḥ in the ayin, and it is not a place of Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The last phrase 'ולא יודע לכל ושכבה בחיקך' appears to quote or allude to I Kings 1:4; its exact syntactic connection to the preceding argument is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:43.761127756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}